d, that after fifty years and more than $2.3 trillion in aid, we have shockingly little to show for it. We preach a gospel of freedom and individual accountability, yet we intrude in the inner workings of other countries through bloated aid bureaucracies--and most of the places in which we've meddled are in fact no better off or are even worse off than they were before. Could it be that we don't know as much as we think we do? -- From publisher description."},"latest_revision":22,"revision":22,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-01T03:28:50.625462"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-02-05T14:27:47.567714"}},{"publishers":["Penguin Group USA, Inc."],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"source_records":["marc_overdrive/InternetArchiveCrMarc-2010-06-11e.mrc:1815414:2244","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-032.mrc:211984004:4630","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-025.mrc:11783772:4630"],"title":"The White Man's Burden","identifiers":{"overdrive":["250ACDE8-ADFB-4429-8F10-38AE0E39D345"]},"isbn_13":["9781429513807","9781429521154"],"covers":[6400076],"physical_format":"Electronic resource","publish_date":"2008","publish_country":"nyu","key":"/books/OL24252382M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL258447A"}],"publish_places":["New York"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL7989576W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["HC59.7 .E22 2006eb"],"oclc_numbers":["458760370"],"latest_revision":6,"revision":6,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2010-06-17T01:32:03.898975"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-12-18T22:17:57.977221"}},{"publishers":["Penguin (Non-Classics)"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["737107"],"goodreads":["33513"]},"subtitle":"Why the West's Efforts to Aid the Rest Have Done So Much Ill and So Little Good","title":"The White Man's Burden","number_of_pages":448,"isbn_13":["9780143038825"],"covers":[111465],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0143038826"],"